--- A list whose first value is empty cannot fail, so it holds no error:
--- a push of a value that can fail, in one branch, is refused where it is
--- assigned (spec, Reassignment), and the list keeps its type in the
--- other branch. The lowering declared the list by the type inference
--- settled on, one that can fail, while the compiled program declared it
--- plain, and the program did not build.
fn gathered[words]
    xs = []
    for w in words
        if w eq ''
            xs = push[xs, 0.0]
        else
            xs = push[xs, float[w]]
    return xs

log[gathered[['1.5', '', '2']]]
bad = gathered[['1', 'x', '3']]
log[bad.ok]
log[bad.reason]
